### HTTP

An HttpRequest object is Django's Python object that represents one complete incoming HTTP request.
When URL pattern is searched, Django creates one HttpRequest object representing this incoming HTTP request, and passes that object to your view.
```
Incoming HTTP Request
├── URL path
├── HTTP method (GET, POST...)
├── Headers
├── Query parameters
├── Request body (if any)
├── Cookies
└── Other request metadata
        │
        ▼
Django creates one HttpRequest instance
        │
        ▼
Passed to your view as `request`
```

**Example of HTTPRequest instance**
the URL + headers + body + other request information packaged into one Python object
```
POST /api/portfolios/?page=2
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "portfolio_name": "Long Term"
}
```